Wine Cellar is a personal tracker for a home wine collection. It was
conceived, designed and written by Charles Adams as an independent personal
project, starting from the family starter template:

  * Built on personally owned hardware, using a personal Anthropic (Claude)
    subscription paid for by the author.
  * Developed in the author's personal GitHub account (eagleadams86).
  * No employer equipment, funding, source code or libraries were used.
  * No employer confidential or proprietary information is present in this
    repository or in the application. Its only built-in data is an invented
    sample cellar generated in the browser; everything a reader types stays in
    their own browser's local storage, or in their own Google account's
    document if they choose to sign in to sync.

